{"decision_id": "P01-005", "book": "Ezek", "model_id": "M8_fable", "chunk_index_in_book": 5, "span": "Ezek.3.12-Ezek.3.15", "boundary_rationale": "Onset: 3:12 וַתִּשָּׂאֵ֣נִי ר֔וּחַ (oshb:Ezek.3.12) (“Then the Spirit lifted me up” (web:Ezek.3.12)) begins the return-transport away from the plain-vision back to the exiles, distinct in texture from the preceding commissioning speech (no address, no imperative - narrated action). 3:14 carries the hand-of-YHWH construct, וְיַד יְהוָ֥ה עָלַ֖י חָזָֽקָה (oshb:Ezek.3.14) ('the hand of YHWH was strong upon me'); it is weighed and NOT read as a fresh vision onset here, in contrast to 1:3 and 3:22 - it sits inside a single continuous journey (lifted up → went in bitterness → came to Tel-abib) with no scene change around it, so it is disclosed as transit texture rather than a hard seam. Close: 3:15, וָאֵשֵׁ֥ב שָׁ֛ם שִׁבְעַ֥ת יָמִ֖ים מַשְׁמִ֥ים בְּתוֹכָֽם (oshb:Ezek.3.15) (“I sat there overwhelmed among them seven days” (web:Ezek.3.15)); no parashah mark is recorded at 3:15, which is not read as counterevidence against the seam. The gap this closes is temporal, not formulaic: 3:16 reopens on “At the end of seven days” (web:Ezek.3.16) with its own strict word-event.", "boundary_evidence_refs": ["oshb:Ezek.3.13 (paseq, single-witness, count-only)", "oshb:Ezek.3.14 (hand-of-YHWH construct present but weighed as transit texture, not an onset, disclosed)", "oshb:Ezek.3.15 (K/Q, checked before quoting: ketiv ואשר / qere וָֽאֵשֵׁ֔ב)", "oshb:Ezek.3.12 [WARRANT-onset:near] transport verb opens the scene", "oshb:Ezek.3.16 [WARRANT-close:far] word-event on the far face", "oshb:Ezek.3.14 [WARRANT-rival:near] 3.13/3.14 transport clause and hand construct", "oshb:Ezek.3.13 [WARRANT-rival:far] 3.13/3.14 wings and wheels, no formula"], "strongest_rejected_alternative": "A cut at 3:13/3:14 is the live rival, weighed here face by face and not taken. Its near face, 3:14, carries two candidate drivers at once: the transport clause וְר֥וּחַ נְשָׂאַ֖ת